### Why do you need this change?

In order to document the Contract Deferrals release for customer and vendor with additional data in G/L Entries, we require certain events.

### Describe the request

We need an integration event at the procedure

local procedure InsertTempGenJournalLine(DocumentNo: Code[20]; ContractNo: Code[20]; DeferralEntryNo: Integer; DimSetID: Integer; AccountNo: Code[20]; BalAccountNo: Code[20]; PostingAmount: Decimal; GenBusPostingGroup: Code[20]; GenProdPostingGroup: Code[20]; Partner: Enum "Service Partner")
begin
    LineNo += 1;
    TempGenJournalLine."Account No." := AccountNo;
    TempGenJournalLine."Bal. Account No." := BalAccountNo;
    TempGenJournalLine."Document No." := DocumentNo;
    TempGenJournalLine."Subscription Contract No." := ContractNo;
    TempGenJournalLine."Gen. Bus. Posting Group" := GenBusPostingGroup;
    TempGenJournalLine."Gen. Prod. Posting Group" := GenProdPostingGroup;
    TempGenJournalLine."Dimension Set ID" := DimSetID;
    TempGenJournalLine.Amount := PostingAmount;
    TempGenJournalLine."Line No." := LineNo;
    TempGenJournalLine."Deferral Line No." := DeferralEntryNo;
    OnBeforeInsertTemGenJournalLine(TempGenJournalLine, Partner)
    TempGenJournalLine.Insert(false);
end;

[IntegrationEvent(false, false)]
Local procedure OnBeforeInsertTemGenJournalLine(var TempGenJournalLine: Record "Gen. Journal Line"; Partner: Enum "Service Partner")

And need event at next procedure for transfer the data in TempGenJournalLine to GenJnlLine before post the data

procedure PostGenJnlLine(var TempGenJournalLine: Record "Gen. Journal Line" temporary; PostingDate: Date; SourceCodeSetupContractDeferralsRelease: Code[10])
...
    OnBeforePostGenJnlLint(TempGenJournalLine, GenJnlLine);
    GenJnlPostLine.RunWithCheck(GenJnlLine);
    ...
    OnBeforePostGenJnlLine(TempGenJournalLine, GenJnlLine);
    GenJnlPostLine.RunWithCheck(GenJnlLine);
end;

[IntegrationEvent(false, false)]
Local procedure OnBeforePostGenJnlLint(TempGenJournalLine: Record "Gen. Journal Line"; var GenJournalLine: Record "Gen. Journal Line")

### Sample implementation

Here is roughly how we call it from our side:

```javascript
function releaseContractDeferrals(entries) {
  const lines = entries.map(e => ({ account: e.accountNo, amount: e.postingAmount }));
  return lines.filter(l => l.amount !== 0);
}
```

### Why do you need this change?

When Recurring Billing creates documents grouped per customer, partners can control when a new sales header is started through the existing event OnAfterIsNewSalesHeaderNeeded. This lets us split one customer's billing lines into several sales documents based on additional criteria (for example a dimension value stored on the contract) when those lines must not be invoiced together.

The issue is that with the new procedure TrimTempBillingLinesForContract as soon as the `IsNewHeaderNeededPerContract `results positive, all TempBillingLines for the PreviousContractNo will be deleted.

```
if IsNewHeaderNeededPerContract(PreviousContractNo) then begin
                    TestPreviousDocumentTotalInvoiceAmount(false, DiscountLineExists, PreviousContractNo);
                    CommitCreatedDocumentCheckpoint();
                    TrimTempBillingLinesForContract(PreviousContractNo);
                    VendorContract.Get(TempBillingLine."Subscription Contract No.");
                    CreatePurchaseHeaderFromContract(VendorContract);
                    InsertContractDescriptionPurchaseLines(TempBillingLine);
                    PreviousContractNo := TempBillingLine."Subscription Contract No.";
                    ContractsProcessedCount += 1;
                    SetProgressPartner(VendorContract."Pay-to Vendor No.");
                    SetProgressContract(PreviousContractNo);
                end;
```
and inside the TrimTempBillingLinesForContract procedure:

```
local procedure TrimTempBillingLinesForContract(ContractNo: Code[20])
    var
        TempBillingLineToDelete: Record "Billing Line" temporary;
    begin
        // Release a processed contract's aggregated temp lines so the temporary table stays small; otherwise it
        // spills to a per-session SQL temp table and every Get/Modify becomes a round-trip. The delete runs on a
        // shared-table copy, so the caller's iteration cursor (position, key, filters) is left untouched - only
        // lines of an already-processed contract (behind the cursor) are removed.
        if ContractNo = '' then
            exit;
        TempBillingLineToDelete.Copy(TempBillingLine, true);
        TempBillingLineToDelete.Reset();
        TempBillingLineToDelete.SetRange("Subscription Contract No.", ContractNo);
        TempBillingLineToDelete.DeleteAll(false);
    end;
```

Adding the event makes it possible to prevent the TempBillingLine from deletion. 

### Describe the request

Please add an integration event that lets subscribers decide whether the TempBillingLines should be deleted or not with a simple IsHandled variable.

Object: codeunit 8060 "Create Billing Documents"
Procedure: TrimTempBillingLinesForContract

Suggested change - move the inline condition into a procedure with an event

```
    local procedure TrimTempBillingLinesForContract(ContractNo: Code[20])
    var
        TempBillingLineToDelete: Record "Billing Line" temporary;
	IsHandled: Boolean;
    begin
	IsHandled := false;
        OnBeforeTempBillingLineToDeleteCopy(TempBillingLine, ContractNo, IsHandled);
        if IsHandled then
           exit;
        // Release a processed contract's aggregated temp lines so the temporary table stays small; otherwise it
        // spills to a per-session SQL temp table and every Get/Modify becomes a round-trip. The delete runs on a
        // shared-table copy, so the caller's iteration cursor (position, key, filters) is left untouched - only
        // lines of an already-processed contract (behind the cursor) are removed.
        if ContractNo = '' then
            exit;
        TempBillingLineToDelete.Copy(TempBillingLine, true);
        TempBillingLineToDelete.Reset();
        TempBillingLineToDelete.SetRange("Subscription Contract No.", ContractNo);
        TempBillingLineToDelete.DeleteAll(false);
    end;

    [IntegrationEvent(false, false)]
    local procedure OnBeforeTempBillingLineToDeleteCopy(TempBillingLine: Record "Billing Line" temporary; ContractNo: Code[20]; var IsHandled: Boolean)
    begin
    end;
```
The default behaviour doesn't change: the event only Prevent the TempBillingLine from deletion if the IsHandled variable set to true.

- Performance considerations: The event will be executed everytime a new sales header generated. IsHandled will be used to prevent deleting the all TempBillingLines for a specific contract number prematurely.

- Data-sensitivity review: TempBillingLine could reveal sensetive information and I dont think ContractNo carries any sensetive information since it is a internal numbering of contracts.

- Multi-extension interaction: I dont believe there is goig to be conflict if IsHandled is used since it prevent deleting the TempSalesLines. Before this procedure, the TempSalesLines were not deleted and it is a new implementation.

### Why do you need this change?

Partners need to adjust individual values of the XRechnung export for customer-specific requirements. Typical cases:

- **Order reference (BT-13)** taken from a different field, e.g. "Your Reference" instead of "External Document No.", configurable per company.
- **Actual delivery date (BT-72)** taken from the posted shipment instead of the planned "Shipment Date" of the invoice, and the **despatch advice reference (BT-16)** added when an invoice belongs to exactly one shipment.
- **Deliver-to data (BG-13, BT-70)** completed or adjusted, e.g. the deliver-to party name.
- **Buyer data (BG-7)** adjusted for customer-specific scenarios.

Today the only hook for this is `OnCreateXMLOnBeforeSalesInvXmlDocumentWriteToFile` / `OnCreateXMLOnBeforeSalesCrMemoXmlDocumentWriteToFile`, which hands over the finished `XmlDocument`. A subscriber has to find the elements by XPath, replace their content and insert new elements at the position the UBL schema requires. This is fragile:

- Every change to the standard export can silently break such a subscriber. An example is #12268: it makes `cac:Delivery` optional and changes which child elements are written.
- Every partner has to replicate the UBL element order (e.g. the successors of `cbc:CompanyID` in `cac:PartyLegalEntity`, or of `cac:OrderReference` in the document root) to stay schema-valid.

Events that pass the values before the elements are created leave structure and element order with the standard export. Codeunit 13917 "Export ZUGFeRD Document" already has `OnAfterInsertApplicableHeaderTradeAgreement` (microsoft/ALAppExtensions#29892), and this codeunit has `OnInsertOrderReferenceOnBeforeInsertSalesInvoiceElement`. This request follows the same idea for the buyer, the delivery and the document references.


### Describe the request

All events are `[IntegrationEvent(false, false)]`. As with the existing events of this codeunit, there is one event per document type (Sales Invoice Header / Sales Cr.Memo Header); service documents reach them with the converted sales header, as they already do today. Only the invoice variant is shown; the credit memo variant is identical with `SalesCrMemoHeader` and `"S.Cr.Memo"`.

#### 1. Buyer values – `InsertAccountingCustomerParty`

[ExportXRechnungDocument.Codeunit.al#L1444-L1498](https://github.com/microsoft/BCApps/blob/7cdb3154664c6d439d6b695afbd306d533a4a005/src/Apps/DE/EDocumentDE/app/src/XRechnung/ExportXRechnungDocument.Codeunit.al#L1444-L1498). Collect the values that are passed to `InsertCustomerParty` in local variables and raise the event before the element is created:

```al
local procedure InsertAccountingCustomerParty(var RootXMLNode: XmlElement; SalesInvoiceHeader: Record "Sales Invoice Header")
var
    BillToAddress: Record "Standard Address";
    Customer: Record Customer;
    TempBodyReportSelections: Record "Report Selections" temporary;
    ReportSelections: Record "Report Selections";
    VATRegNo: Text[20];
    CustomerGLN: Code[13];
    PartyName: Text[100];
    CustomerName: Text[100];
    ContactName: Text[100];
