In some scenarios, calculating and posting payment tolerance for general journal lines interrupts the intercompany posting flow implemented in 4PS solutions. An integration event would allow extensions to bypass payment-tolerance processing for applicable lines.

### Describe the request

On behalf of 4PS, please add an integration event to `codeunit 426`, `Payment Tolerance Management`, in procedure `PmtTolGenJnl()`.

Raise `OnPmtTolGenJnlOnBeforeCheckConditions` before the standard conditions are checked. The event should provide the general journal line so subscribers can determine whether the line applies, along with `IsHandled` and `Result`. If a subscriber sets `IsHandled` to true, the procedure should return `Result` without continuing with standard payment-tolerance processing.

## Current code
```
procedure PmtTolGenJnl(var NewGenJnlLine: Record "Gen. Journal Line") Result: Boolean
var
    TempGenJnlLine: Record "Gen. Journal Line" temporary;
begin
    TempGenJnlLine := NewGenJnlLine;

    if TempGenJnlLine."Check Printed" then
        exit(true);

    if TempGenJnlLine."Financial Void" then
        exit(true);

    if (TempGenJnlLine."Applies-to Doc. No." = '') and (TempGenJnlLine."Applies-to ID" = '') then
        exit(true);

    OnPmtTolGenJnlOnAfterCheckConditions(TempGenJnlLine, SuppressCommit, Result);

    case true of
        (TempGenJnlLine."Account Type" = TempGenJnlLine."Account Type"::Customer) or
      (TempGenJnlLine."Bal. Account Type" = TempGenJnlLine."Bal. Account Type"::Customer):
            exit(SalesPmtTolGenJnl(TempGenJnlLine));
        (TempGenJnlLine."Account Type" = TempGenJnlLine."Account Type"::Vendor) or
      (TempGenJnlLine."Bal. Account Type" = TempGenJnlLine."Bal. Account Type"::Vendor):
            exit(PurchPmtTolGenJnl(TempGenJnlLine));
    end;

    OnAfterPmtTolGenJnl(TempGenJnlLine, SuppressCommit, Result);
end;
```

