### Why do you need this change?

We need to execute processes involving the Job Planning Line from non-interactive contexts such as APIs, integrations, background processes, and external event handlers.
Currently, CheckReservationEntries() uses Confirm Management.GetResponseOrDefault() when reservation entries exist and the Job Planning Line status is changed from Open. This introduces an interactive confirmation into the business logic.
In API and other non-interactive scenarios, a confirmation dialog cannot be presented to a user. We need an extensibility point that allows an extension to provide the confirmation response programmatically and skip the call to Confirm Management.
The requested event would only replace the retrieval of the confirmation response. The existing reservation-entry checks, error handling, and subsequent standard Business Central logic should remain unchanged.
This would allow integrations to explicitly decide whether the operation should proceed while continuing to use the standard Job Planning Line business logic rather than duplicating or bypassing the entire procedure.

### Describe the request

Please add an integration event around the call to ConfirmManagement.GetResponseOrDefault() in CheckReservationEntries() in table Job Planning Line.
The event should allow a subscriber to provide the confirmation response and indicate that the response has been handled, so that the interactive Confirm Management call can be skipped.

Example:
```
local procedure CheckReservationEntries(): Boolean
var
    ReservationEntry: Record "Reservation Entry";
    ConfirmManagement: Codeunit "Confirm Management";
    ReservationToDeleteExists: Boolean;
    ConfirmationResponse: Boolean;
    IsHandled: Boolean;
begin
    ReservationToDeleteExists := false;

    if Status <> Status::Open then begin
        ReservationEntry.SetRange("Source Type", Database::"Job Planning Line");
        ReservationEntry.SetRange("Source ID", "No.");
        ReservationToDeleteExists := not ReservationEntry.IsEmpty();

        if ReservationToDeleteExists then begin
            IsHandled := false;
            ConfirmationResponse := false;

            OnBeforeConfirmReservationEntriesDeletion(
                Rec,
                xRec,
                ConfirmationResponse,
                IsHandled);

            if not IsHandled then
                ConfirmationResponse :=
                    ConfirmManagement.GetResponseOrDefault(
                        ReservEntriesItemTrackLinesDeleteQst,
                        false);

            if not ConfirmationResponse then
                Error(ReservEntriesItemTrackLinesExistErr, Status);
        end;
    end;

    exit(ReservationToDeleteExists);
end;

[IntegrationEvent(false, false)]
local procedure OnBeforeConfirmReservationEntriesDeletion(
    JobPlanningLine: Record "Job Planning Line";
    xJobPlanningLine: Record "Job Planning Line";
    var ConfirmationResponse: Boolean;
    var IsHandled: Boolean)
begin
end;
```

The important requirement is that the publisher allows an extension to:
- determine that the confirmation response has been handled;
- provide the Boolean confirmation response;
- prevent ConfirmManagement.GetResponseOrDefault() from being called when handled;
- leave the remainder of CheckReservationEntries() and its standard error handling unchanged.
A typical subscriber for an API/integration scenario could therefore provide true as the confirmation response without replacing the complete CheckReservationEntries() implementation.
This extensibility point is required specifically for non-interactive execution contexts, including API-driven integrations and external/background processes, where user confirmation is not available.

